Fixed. `pytest -q`: **15 passed, 0 failed**. Only `src/` changed; nothing under `tests/`.

What was wrong per module:

- **`src/auth.py`** — `has_permission` compared case-sensitively (now lowercases both sides); `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of `or`, so it required admin *and* owner.
- **`src/inventory.py`** — four bugs: mutable default `{}` shared state across instances (now `None` → fresh dict, copied on init); `add` overwrote stock instead of accumulating; `reserve` rejected `qty == available` due to `>=` (now `>`); `release` let reserved go negative (now raises `ValueError` when release exceeds reserved).
- **`src/text_utils.py`** — `slugify` didn't lowercase and `replace("--", "-")` couldn't collapse runs longer than two separators (now only appends a separator when the last char isn't one, then strips edges); `truncate` returned `max_len + len(suffix)` characters (now truncates to `max_len - len(suffix)` before appending).

No `skip`/`xfail` markers anywhere in `src/`.
